# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines:
# a signature OpenSSL made is accepted inside a PD, and one bit
# changed in the message, the signature or the public key, or an r of zero,
# is refused. Each check's time is printed too ("took N us"), but varies
# from run to run, so only the bound on the slowest is checked.
NOWAYOS: signature-check: starting
NOWAYOS: signature-check: OpenSSL's signature: accepted
NOWAYOS: signature-check: one bit of the message changed: refused: the signature does not match the key and message
NOWAYOS: signature-check: one bit of the signature changed: refused: the signature does not match the key and message
NOWAYOS: signature-check: one bit of the public key changed: refused: the public key is not a point on P-256
NOWAYOS: signature-check: r of zero: refused: the signature's r is zero
NOWAYOS: signature-check: every check took under 1 s
NOWAYOS: signature-check: done

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring
# match), including in the settle period after the last line above: a fault
# reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic, or a
# check over its bound.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!over 1 s
